^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-07-27] revise — revive plan from archive; multi-client doctrine with vscode-lsp-roadmap
 >>[2026-07-27] observe — neovim already has OperatorFreq/Phase/Temperature/FormSeq commands; capability honesty still required
 >>[2026-07-27] observe — index.spw wonder blocks + $% metrics are authored but editor-inert
 >>[2026-07-27] decide — mass/path/open-question diagnostics land on server first; Neovim only projects
 >>[2026-07-27] decide — :SpwPlan thin-reads wip frames; no second Spw parser in Lua
 >>[2026-07-27] taste — builtins first; telescope optional never required
 >>[2026-07-27] revise — shape-syntax-ecology; :SpwProfile; screenshot dual-read; dialect statusline
 >>[2026-08-24 12:58] observe — the CLI now exposes tokens, structure, and trace as one progressive product with spans, provenance, omissions, elapsed time, and event counts; Neovim lacks a native projection of that scientific receipt.
 >>[2026-08-24 12:59] decide — add :SpwInspect as a projection, never a Lua parser: file-backed CLI fallback may land first, while unsaved buffer, selection, and block-local work require an earned shared server or stdin protocol.
 >>[2026-08-24 13:00] taste — scientific/editor and broad-audience/site surfaces may differ in density and interaction, but they share product identity, provenance, loss receipts, and local-first privacy boundaries.
 >>[2026-09-30 16:54] revise — the evidence-state audit may proceed. New wrappers and :SpwInspect expansion wait while lsp-custom-request-completions holds the method matrix for language and cost scrutiny.
 >>[2026-10-12 12:48] observe — A mounted consumer's editor asks (pin 229aedcf) name no Neovim work. Derived projections are in PLAN.md: LSP-level rows arrive through native mechanisms, chrome rows are not ported. navigation.lua and completion.lua extract citations and aliases with Lua patterns, the client-side twin of the server regex-first disagreement the consumer measured.
 >>[2026-10-12 12:48] decide — No new :Spw wrappers or custom requests follow from these asks; the held method matrix still governs. The next step is unchanged.
 >>[2026-10-12 15:25] revise — Commits named per the convention in 90c58bbc: 0 landed, 8 planned, 0 dropped.
 >>[2026-10-12 20:09] implement — Landed in 1bb4f68d: navigation and completion ask the attached server first; :SpwInspect, :SpwFingerprint, :SpwMemory, :SpwPerf, :SpwProject and :SpwQuest. The creator's own config was updated so the plugin's module loads and one server attaches.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:39] observe — Owner screenshot, 2026-10-13: nvim on the repo-root index.spw resolves root refs inline as virtual text and shows wonder metric counts; it raises nothing for &[@profile, @docs], where @profile is not a declared root, and the roots still name lib/spw-v0.2.0-alpha and src/seed. Journal-aware features from caches-living-tree land in the LSP so this host gets them without new :Spw wrappers.
 >>[2026-10-13 11:59] revise — 1bb4f68d landed six CLI-backed :Spw commands while the matrix hold stood; CLI-backed commands are exempt, since they wrap no spw/* method. demote_phantom_wrappers is moot (every called method is handled). The open gaps are the empty Neovim cells for tokens, inlay hints, and lenses in hosts/host-parity-matrix.spw; audit_surfaces fills them and feeds lsp-custom-request-completions capability_matrix.
 >>[2026-10-13 17:16] implement — Landed 198f6875 and bdd48943 at the owner's request for Neovim parity with the VS Code commit work, without a slot reserved first. The server now registers file watchers with any client that takes dynamic registration; headless Neovim against the real server receives both watchers. In Neovim, gf follows a commit link when there is no definition; :SpwCommit opens a read-only git show buffer named spw-commit://; :SpwCommitFiles fills the quickfix list; code lenses refresh on attach and edits; vim.g.spw_lsp_inlay_hints and vim.g.spw_lsp_codelens turn those off; commitRef links to @number. commit-smoke.lua fails at gf and at code lenses with main's lsp_nav.lua and lsp.lua.
 >>[2026-10-26 12:29] observe — audit_surfaces evidence, 2026-10-26, headless Neovim 0.11.6 with the real server: the built-in client paints spw-lsp semantic tokens at priority 125 over syntax/spw.vim, so the per-sigil syntax groups show only where no token covers. vim.treesitter.language.inspect finds no spw parser, so queries/spw/*.scm never ran, though the README advertises them.
 >>[2026-10-26 12:29] observe — Navigation and learning gaps, read 2026-10-26: the only structural motions are [d and ]d; no text objects; no doc/, so :help spw finds nothing; 30 separate :Spw commands and no hub; folds come from syntax regex while the server serves foldingRange. The server outline is token-driven and hierarchical and names each symbol detail (frame, action, probe, anchor), so motions and frame text objects need no new server method.
 >>[2026-10-26 12:29] decide — Spw moves as Vim moves. Motions and frame text objects read textDocument/documentSymbol; expression and facet text objects read a new textDocument/selectionRange; :help is generated from the operator table and commands.lua. Lua still parses nothing.
}

^["open"]{
 ?[statusline]: "Ship optional statusline.lua helper or document lualine snippet only?"
 ?[probe_method]: "Earn spw/probe vs encode probe results only as diagnostics?"
 ?[source_product_transport]: "Should unsaved and range inspection use one earned LSP request, a shared stdin envelope, or both over the same SourceProduct contract?"
 ?[motion_keys]: "Do structural motions take ]] and [[ (Vim section motions, which readers expect to mean the top-level unit) with ]a and ]? beside them, or one prefix for every Spw motion? ]s is taken by spelling."
 ?[help_generator_home]: "Does the :help generator live in scripts/ beside the other generators or inside the extension, and does it read the table through the seed package or a JSON export a Lua-only install can ship?"
}

^["commits"]{
 ~[audit_surfaces]: "![neovim] *audit[surfaces] — real-lsp-smoke records whether the built-in client paints spw-lsp semantic tokens, inlay hints, and code lenses; results fill lsp-custom-request-completions ~[capability_matrix] (hosts/host-parity-matrix.spw, editor_hosts_parity)"
 ~[audit_mounted_consumer]: "![neovim] *audit[mounted-consumer] — startup, roots, failure behavior"
 ~[readme_health_honesty]: ".[neovim] — README + health honesty for mount/workbench discovery"
 ~[project_mass_diagnostics]: "&[neovim] — project mass/path diagnostics + exact-only code actions (after LSP emits them)"
 ~[plan_statusline_profile]: "^[neovim] — :SpwPlan / optional statusline + reading_profile setting"
 .[project_source_products](1bb4f68d): "&[neovim] — :SpwInspect projects the shared source products (tokens, structure, trace) for a file or a selection through the CLI"
 ~[smoke_contracts]: "![neovim] — smoke for wonder hover and diagnostics only; lsp-route-smoke.lua and instrument-smoke.lua (1bb4f68d) already cover refs and source products"
 .[lsp_first_navigation](1bb4f68d): "&[neovim] — gf, :SpwOpenRef and completion use the attached LSP and fall back to Lua patterns only when none is attached (answers ?[lua_extractors])"
 .[quest_command](1bb4f68d): "&[neovim] — :SpwQuest opens the quest panels and :SpwQuest check runs spw quest --check on the current line"
 .[server_file_watchers](198f6875): "&[lsp] — the server registers its file watchers with every client that takes dynamic registration, so Neovim reports .spw changes and folder deletes too"
 .[commit_links_and_lenses](bdd48943): "&[neovim] — commit links open in Neovim, code lenses draw, and inlay hints and the commitRef color are configurable"
 ~[drop_treesitter_queries]: "&[neovim] — delete queries/spw/*.scm and their README section; no spw parser exists, so they never ran"
 ~[structural_motions]: "&[neovim] — ]] and [[ step frames, ]a and [a anchors, ]? and [? probes, read from textDocument/documentSymbol details; counts and the jumplist work as for any motion; no Lua parsing"
 ~[frame_text_objects]: "&[neovim] — af and if select a frame and its body from its documentSymbol range, in operator-pending and visual mode"
 ~[outline_go]: "&[neovim] — gO opens the outline in the location list, as :help and :Man do"
 ~[lsp_folds]: "&[neovim] — folds from vim.lsp.foldexpr() while the server is attached; foldmethod=syntax only without it"
 ~[selection_range]: "&[lsp] — textDocument/selectionRange from the parse: token, expression, facet, frame, file; VS Code expand-selection gets it too; a capability matrix row in lsp-custom-request-completions"
 ~[expression_text_objects]: "&[neovim] — ae and ie select an expression, ak and ik a facet, from selectionRange"
 ~[operator_highlight_links]: "&[neovim] — link each @lsp.typemod.operator.<word> group to its per-sigil syntax group, so semantic tokens paint by operator; needs editor-reading-hierarchy operator_modifiers"
 ~[spw_hub]: "&[neovim] — one :Spw command with completion grouped read, sense and mutate, as spw help groups the CLI; the :Spw* commands stay as aliases"
 ~[generated_help]: "#[neovim] — doc/spw.txt generated from the operator table, commands.lua and the keymap table, with a tag per command, mapping and sigil; a check mode fails on drift"
 ~[quest_motions]: "&[neovim] — each :SpwQuest step practises one motion or text object on the open file (shares onboarding-quest)"
}

